# Line endings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: several shell scripts in infra/ are mounted straight into Linux containers
# (infra/vault/bootstrap.sh, infra/minio/bootstrap.sh, the smoke suites). Checked out with CRLF on
# Windows, `set -eu` becomes `set -eu\r`, and the container dies on line 4 with
#
#     /bootstrap.sh: line 4: set: -: invalid option
#
# The Vault and MinIO bootstraps then never run: no AppRole, no buckets, and every service that
# depends on them fails later for reasons that look nothing like a line ending. Fixing the working
# copy is not enough — with core.autocrlf=true git normalises it straight back on the next commit,
# so the fix has to live here.

# Let git decide for ordinary text, so Windows editors still see CRLF where it does not matter.
* text=auto

# Anything executed by a Linux shell or copied into an image MUST be LF, on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Read inside containers or by tools that are strict about it.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers stay CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
